'' A DEFINITION joins its DECLARE rather than chaining beside it. Without that they were
'' two symbols with identical signatures, so every call to a procedure that was declared
'' and then defined -- most real programs -- was AMBIGUOUS and resolved to nothing.
''
'' It went unnoticed because of what the corpus looks like: fbcunit declares its
'' procedures in a header and defines them in a library fbx never compiles, and the
'' overload gate's probes are all bodiless declarations.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --check tests/symbols/src/declare-define.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 1 calls resolved, 0 ambiguous
